meta {
  name: Create Product - Missing SKU (422)
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

post {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "label": "Test No SKU"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 422
  res.body.errors[0].description: contains sku
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-07 against "David's Dev Account". Trigger case
  only -- omits the one required field (`sku`) so nothing is created.
  **Do not add a valid `sku` to this request** -- real product
  create/delete testing belongs to Phase 2b (`02-Products-v3`'s own
  future extension), which uses disposable scratch products, not this
  Phase 0 validation probe.

  ## 422 shape confirmed
  `{"data":[],"errors":[{"name":"InputDTOValidationError","description":
  "sku: Field required"}]}` -- a flat `errors` array of
  `{name, description}` objects, where `description` is a free-text
  `"<field>: <message>"` string naming the missing field directly. This is
  a **different envelope** from:
  - The 401 auth error (`{"error":{"msg":...,"errors":[{"field":
    "http_status_code","msg":401}]}}` -- nested under `error`, and the
    `errors[].field` value is mislabeled).
  - FastAPI's own default `HTTPValidationError` shape
    (`{"detail":[{"loc":[...],"msg":...,"type":...}]}`), which does NOT
    appear here at all -- Plytix wraps validation errors in its own
    custom envelope consistently across at least these two endpoints.
}
